    "## 1. Join Accessibility Datasets into Spatial Grid\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Technical Methodology & Workflow Overview\n",
    "1. **Spatial Boundary Ingestion**: Load the YKR spatial grid dataset for the Helsinki Metropolitan Area.\n",
    "2. **Accessibility Matrix Integration**: Import origin-destination (O/D) travel time matrices for key commercial nodes (Itis and Myyrmanni).\n",
    "3. **Attribute Selection & Data Hygiene**: Extract modal travel times (`pt_r_t` for public transport, `car_r_t` for private vehicles), standardise column naming per target location, convert missing-data sentinel values (`-1`) to null values (`NaN`), and perform a relational join with grid geometries.\n",
    "4. **Travel Time Classification**: Bin modal accessibility figures into 5-minute threshold breaks (up to 60 minutes) using `mapclassify.UserDefined` to compare spatial coverage.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "### Spatial Data Source & Reference Framework\n",
    "The spatial grid boundaries are based on the standardized YKR grid system (`YKR_grid_EPSG3067.gpkg`), maintained by the Finnish Environment Institute (SYKE). This coordinate reference system serves as the foundational spatial unit for urban geography and spatial accessibility research developed at the Digital Geography Lab, University of Helsinki.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
